# POC3 multi-agent SDD + TDD

**Active workstream:** `poc3/` · backlog `.docs3/todo.md` · hub `.docs3/plans/planning.spec.MD`

POC-1 (`poc/`) and POC-2 (`poc2/`) are **frozen**. Do not edit them. Do not open tasks against them. Reference only (feel / coverage checklist).

Docs2 (`.docs2/`) is a **coverage checklist only** — not inherited architecture.

## Hub summary (docs3 v0.1.0)

English design source of truth. Key locks:

| Lock | Rule |
|---|---|
| **Summary Sheet only** | Frame systems read `ENE` `SHD` `DEF` `MIT` `SPD` `S_D` `S_R` `REG` `LVL` `HP` + integrity state. Full Sheet recalc is event-driven (`CHAR-05`). Hits use precomputed `MIT` (`D24`). |
| **Death** | Integrity 0 = **DRIFTING**; next hit = **DEAD** → run over (`CHAR-04`). |
| **Slots** | 12 Special (incl. Primary/Secondary weapon) + 21 Generic + 21 Effect (`CHAR-01`). |
| **Damage** | Mitigate by `DEF/10` → Shield → Integrity; ship–ship = other `HP/2` (`CHAR-06`). |
| **Classes** | **Tanker** · Warrior · Rogue (+ Special). Docs2 “Tank” = Tanker. |
| **Enemy SM** | `EnterGate` · `FindGroup` · `LoopBack` · `Flee` · `Fury` (`ENEMY-02`). |
| **Squad** | 1–8 · formations `V`/`Circle`/`CircleII–IV`/`LineDivers` · independent squad SM (`SQUAD-*`). |
| **Boot** | All flow scenes on the **shared canvas** (`D23`): Login → Start → Title → Run; Pause is a canvas UI layer (`SCENE-05`). |
| **IDs** | `CHAR-` · `ENEMY-` · `SQUAD-` · `SCENE-` (stable). System classes: `*Manager` only (`D22`, hub §2.6). |

Full decisions: hub §3 (`D01`–`D18`). Requirement index: hub §7.

## Agents (disjoint ownership)

| Agent | Spec sections | Code | Forbidden |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Orchestrator** | header, Scope, Requires, sign-off | `.docs3/todo.md` checkoff; refuse open `requires` | numbers, THREE, tests |
| **Programming / Three.js** | Contract, Fields, Rules, View | classes, `extends THREE.*`, `dispose()`, pools | BALANCE values, skipping tests |
| **Game Design** | BALANCE / feel / leveling / graphics | `BALANCE` numbers, palette, cadence | class shape, tests, literals outside BALANCE |
| **TDD** | Acceptance cases | `{subject}.test.ts` written **red** first; runs `npm run test` | production implementation |

Template (when specs exist): `.docs3/specs/_template.spec.ts`. Until then, Orchestrator still owns order and DoD from this rule + hub.

## Order on every card

1. Orchestrator opens/fills the spec (Scope + Requires) from the hub ID.
2. Programming fills contract / memory / view.
3. Game Design fills BALANCE + feel + leveling + graphics.
4. TDD names cases and writes the failing test file.
5. Programming implements until green. TDD re-runs `verify`. Game Design play-checks. Orchestrator ticks DoD in `.docs3/todo.md`.

A spec with an empty agent section is incomplete. `N/A` is allowed; blank is not.

## Implementation gates

- Spec before code. Tests before implementation.
- `interface` + `class`, one public class per `kebab-case.ts`. Domain owners use `*Manager` — never `*Controller` or `*Resolver` (`D22`).
- `update(dt)` = logic; `syncRender()` = transforms/opacity/material only.
- Gameplay numbers only in `BALANCE`. Frame code must not recompute Full Sheet math.
- Zero per-frame allocation on hot paths.
- Audio is always `SoundManager` (volumes, mute, AI VO, cue log).
- `npm run verify` in `poc3/` must be green before Orchestrator marks done.
- Follow `.docs3/todo.md` theme order — do not skip upstream themes.
